# Reviewing changes in `middleware/`

The unified reviewer (`prompts/codeReviewer/v3/`) loads **`middleware/REVIEW.md`** for
any changed path under `middleware/`. That map cites rule IDs from
`middleware/AGENTS.md` and `frontend/AGENTS.md` (e.g. `F-R2`, the
BFF-holds-no-cloud-credentials rule, `trace_id` passthrough) — it never restates the rule
text.

Deterministic checks that fire here first (precedence over LLM):
- FD3 `check_secrets_in_public_env` — the credentialed BFF must hold no cloud credentials
  (critical).
- FD1 F-R2 — SDK imports confined to `middleware/adapters/` (LLM-judged).
- FD1 `trace_id` flows verbatim, never generated here (LLM-judged).

Dispatch the reviewer:

```bash
python -m meta.code_reviewer --from-git-diff --git-base HEAD --prompt-version v3 --output review.json
```

Deterministic findings are the gate; the v3 LLM judge is WI-8 certified (TPR/TNR = 1.0) so LLM verdicts are gate-grade for the routed LLM-only rules — re-record when the judge model changes.
Full contract: `docs/skills/code-review/SKILL.md`.
